Roast.pet Frontier Stack =E2=80=94 1 useful find

Murf Falcon 2 =E2=80=94 TEST for interactive Roast.pet voice; WATCH upcomin=
g upgrade

Fresh signal: Murf AI disclosed this week that its current Falcon 2
conversational voice model is priced at about $0.01 per audio minute,
targets sub-200ms latency, supports 150+ voices across 35+ languages, and
that an upgraded Falcon variant is planned within roughly three weeks. This
is a materially cheaper live-voice option than the $0.05/minute GPT-Live-1
voice layer captured in the previous scan, although this run did not
establish equivalent full-duplex reasoning/tool semantics.

Source: Financial Express, published Sep 14 2026:
https://www.financialexpress.com/life/technology/murf-ai-to-launch-upgraded=
-variant-of-voice-model/4338593/

Capability relevant to Roast.pet: cheap low-latency speech for the
interactive QR experience (=E2=80=9Cscan card =E2=86=92 talk to your pet =
=E2=86=92 pet roasts you
back=E2=80=9D).
Inputs/outputs: conversational audio/text context =E2=86=92 streaming speec=
h.
API/install: Murf hosted API; no self-hosted weights established.
Pricing: reported $0.01/audio minute for Falcon 2.
Commercial/license: hosted commercial service; no open-weight license
established.
Privacy: cloud processing; pass PetPersona/text/audio only, not original
customer pet uploads.
Constraints: primarily positioned for conversational voice; benchmark
comedic expressiveness and interruption behavior rather than assuming
parity with GPT-Live-1. Upcoming upgrade is announced rather than released.
Exact use case: LiveRoast voice layer behind PetPersona, with visual
animation handled separately.
Smallest prototype: identical 20 two-minute PetPersona conversations
through Murf Falcon 2 and GPT-Live-1. Measure first-audio latency,
interruption quality, punchlines/minute, voice expressiveness and billed
cost.
Decision: TEST Falcon 2; WATCH the announced upgrade.

TOP 5 STACK CHANGES TO TEST NOW

   1. P-Video-2-Pro Speed for cheap best-of-N drafts.
   2. LongCat vs H3 Max vs Wan 2.7 on actual cats/dogs.
   3. Local pet cutout =E2=86=92 QC =E2=86=92 Knockout fallback.
   4. Multi-take TTS =E2=86=92 comedy ranking =E2=86=92 video =E2=86=92 aud=
iovisual QC.
   5. Murf Falcon 2 vs GPT-Live-1 for interactive PetPersona voice.

CHEAPEST meaningful capability improvement
Local segmentation remains effectively $0 marginal inference. For
interactive voice, Murf=E2=80=99s reported ~$0.01/minute is the new low-cos=
t
benchmark from this scan.

BIGGEST CAPABILITY SHOCK THIS HOUR
No new image/video foundation-model release cleared the novelty and
verification bar. The useful economic delta is live conversational speech
at roughly one cent per minute, with another Murf model upgrade imminent.

CONCRETE STACK SIMPLIFICATION
Keep PetPersona independent from the speech provider: LiveRoast =E2=86=92
VoiceSession interface =E2=86=92 Murf/GPT-Live provider adapter =E2=86=92 o=
ptional visual
